    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d450">

                <pb facs="0564" n="306" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg306"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/1257½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grey</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the British
                        Embassy in Washington </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1915-01-13">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 13, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Left at the Department of State June
                        12.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I cannot give a pledge that all ships now in prize court will be released on bail
                    being offered because decision must rest with judge, but you may make it known
                    that in order to relieve a shortage of tonnage H. M. G. are anxious to withdraw
                    ships as little as possible from carrying trade and will therefore not oppose
                    release on bail of ships now in prize court if bail is offered.</p>
                <p>Only seven neutral vessels are at present in prize court and only five ships are
                    detained here in addition at this moment for examination as to character and
                    true destination of their cargo; one of these will probably be released almost
                    immediately and no one of them is under American flag.</p>
                <p>It would perhaps be well if this were publicly known and I am giving information
                    to press here.</p>
                <closer>[File copy not signed]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
